BotW Save Manager for Mac
=========================

This program is a Rust rewrite of the save conversion logic of BotW Save
Manager, a Windows/Linux desktop and console application:

    https://github.com/DeltaJordan/BotW-Save-Manager

    Copyright (C) the BotW Save Manager authors and contributors,
    including Jordan Marine (DeltaJordan) and Arch Leaders.

BotW Save Manager is itself a fork of WemI0's BOTW_SaveConv, which supplied the
original format research. The upstream project is licensed under the GNU Affero
General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE.md, which is the upstream licence
text, byte for byte).

What was taken from upstream
-----------------------------

Ported from the C# implementation in BotwSaveManager.Core/BotwSave.cs (the
`Headers`, `Versions`, `Items` and `Hashes` tables and the `ConvertPlatform`
loop):

  - the byte-swap algorithm used on save files, including the special case for
    the 65536-byte trackblock files;
  - the table of 44 field hashes whose values need no swap;
  - the table of 60 item-name hashes treated as text;
  - the version-code to game-version table and the platform header shapes.

These are the parts of this project that are not original work. Everything
below is a change made for this rewrite and is not present upstream.

What this rewrite adds
----------------------

  - A reader for the record-table container shared by option.sav, game_data.sav
    and caption.sav (version word, two fixed words, then { hash, value } pairs
    terminated by 0xffffffff), plus a downgrade path that drops the fields
    introduced after Wii U 1.5.0 and retags the header to 0x471b. Upstream
    requires both sides to be on the same game version ("upgrade/downgrade
    untested"); this avoids that by performing the downgrade.
  - A caption.sav reader that reports the save-select information: write time,
    play time, region, and manual/autosave plus normal/Master Mode.
  - Per-file platform detection, so a slot that already uses the target byte
    order is copied instead of being swapped twice.
  - Input is opened read-only, output must not pre-exist, the whole conversion
    happens in a hidden temporary folder and is renamed into place only after
    the result is re-read and validated.
  - A macOS fallback for the final rename, which some protected folders
    (~/Downloads, ~/Desktop) refuse even though writing is allowed.
  - An English-language CLI with a dry-run mode and per-slot reporting.

The record-table hashes and the downgrade field lists were derived by diffing
real v1.5 / v1.6 / v1.8-v1.9 saves, and cross-checked against the format notes
of https://github.com/fabiangonzalezdev/Universal-BOTW-Save-Manager

